# Rank 1146 / CVE-2025-53106: Graylog's token-creation endpoint checked
# whether the REQUESTING user could create tokens for themselves, then used
# that answer to authorize creating a token for whichever OTHER user the URL
# named, so any user holding the token-create permission for their own
# account could mint API tokens for arbitrary other accounts by changing the
# path parameter (CWE-285).
#
# UsersResource's token-creation handler in
# .../rest/resources/users/UsersResource.java loaded `futureOwner` from the
# `userId` path parameter (the account the token would belong to), then
# called `isPermitted(USERS_TOKENCREATE, currentUser.getName())`, checking
# the permission against `currentUser`, the account making the request, not
# `futureOwner`, the account being acted on.
#
# Pool commit 9215b8f1fd32 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK, its changelog entry
# names the advisory). It removes the `currentUser` lookup entirely and
# checks `isPermitted(USERS_TOKENCREATE, futureOwner.getName())`, so the
# permission check now runs against the actual target of the operation. No
# pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. Scanning either revision reports the same
# thirteen findings, all unrelated CSRF-shaped noise; nothing labels the
# subject mismatch itself. code.IdorPolicyReview is the nearest concept by
# theme, an authorization check missing the current-principal ownership
# constraint its own resource lookup should carry, and it already has PHP
# and JavaScript bindings, but none for Java, and its stated condition is
# about a lookup or delete missing an ownership constraint entirely rather
# than a check present but evaluated against the wrong principal (self
# instead of the operation's actual target) -- a related but narrower shape
# this concept does not quite name either.
#
# No definition change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1146: the permission check runs against the requester, not the token's future owner"
  lang java
  file UsersResource.java
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  package org.graylog2.rest.resources.users;

  public class UsersResource extends RestResource {
      public Response createToken(@PathParam("userId") String userId, GenerateTokenTTL body) {
          final User futureOwner = loadUserById(userId);
          final User currentUser = getCurrentUser();

          if (currentUser == null) {
              throw new ForbiddenException("Not allowed to create tokens for unknown user.");
          }
          if (!isPermitted(USERS_TOKENCREATE, currentUser.getName())) {
              throw new ForbiddenException(currentUser.getName() + " is not allowed to create token.");
          }

          return createTokenForUser(futureOwner);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1146: the permission check runs against the token's actual future owner"
  lang java
  file UsersResource.java
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  package org.graylog2.rest.resources.users;

  public class UsersResource extends RestResource {
      public Response createToken(@PathParam("userId") String userId, GenerateTokenTTL body) {
          final User futureOwner = loadUserById(userId);

          if (!isPermitted(USERS_TOKENCREATE, futureOwner.getName())) {
              throw new ForbiddenException("You are not allowed to create a token for user " + futureOwner.getName() + ".");
          }

          return createTokenForUser(futureOwner);
      }
  }
  ```
